.TH GFP-COMMIT 1 "September 2026" "gfp-cli 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gfp-commit \- Record staged or working changes into a Perforce pending changelist
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gfp commit
[\fB\-m\fR \fIMESSAGE\fR | \fB\-\-message\fR \fIMESSAGE\fR]
[\fB\-a\fR | \fB\-\-all\fR]
[\fB\-\-amend\fR]
[\fB\-c\fR \fICL\fR | \fB\-\-cl\fR \fICL\fR]
[\fIfiles...\fR]
.br
.B gfp ci
\fIoptions...\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gfp commit
translates the standard Git commit mental model into native Perforce Helix Core pending changelists.

In Git, committing records a snapshot of the staged index into the local Git repository history. In Perforce, work in progress is organized into numbered pending changelists on the server.
.B gfp commit
creates a new numbered pending changelist (\fBp4 change \-i\fR) with the provided description and automatically associates the opened files into that changelist (\fBp4 reopen \-c \fICL\fR).

.SS Selective File Commits & Rollback Safety
When target file paths are specified (\fBgfp commit \fIfile1 file2\fR \fB\-m "\fIMESSAGE\fB"\fR),
.B gfp
pre-validates the target files against currently opened workspace files. If target files cannot be reconciled or reopened into the newly created changelist,
.B gfp
automatically rolls back and purges the empty changelist (\fBp4 change \-d \fICL\fR), ensuring no dangling or empty changelists are orphaned on the Perforce server.

.SS Amending Changelists
Passing
.B \-\-amend
allows developers to update the description of the most recent pending changelist (or the changelist ID passed via \fB\-c\fR / \fB\-\-cl\fR). If files are also specified or \fB\-a\fR is used, those files are reopened into the changelist being amended.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-m " " \fIMESSAGE\fR ", " \-\-message " " \fIMESSAGE\fR
The commit description text. If omitted,
.B gfp
creates the changelist with a default timestamped summary.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Automatically reconcile all modified and deleted workspace files (\fBp4 reconcile\fR) before creating or updating the changelist.
.TP
.B \-\-amend
Amend the description or file list of an existing pending changelist instead of creating a new one.
.TP
.BR \-c " " \fICL\fR ", " \-\-cl " " \fICL\fR
Specify the exact pending changelist ID to amend. When omitted with \fB\-\-amend\fR,
.B gfp
targets the most recent pending changelist owned by the active client workspace.
.TP
.I files...
Optional file or directory paths to include in the changelist. When omitted, all currently opened files in the default changelist are included.

.SH LIFECYCLE HOOKS
.TP
.BR pre\-commit ", " pre_commit
Executed prior to changelist creation or amendment. If the hook script exits with a non-zero exit code, changelist creation is aborted immediately.
.TP
.BR post\-commit ", " post_commit
Executed immediately after the changelist has been successfully created or amended.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B Commit currently opened files into a new pending changelist:
.nf
$ gfp commit -m "feat(parser): add JSON configuration loader"
.fi

.TP
.B Stage all workspace modifications and commit in a single step:
.nf
$ gfp commit -a -m "refactor: simplify client workspace resolution"
.fi

.TP
.B Commit only specific modified files:
.nf
$ gfp commit src/auth.py tests/test_auth.py -m "feat: user authentication"
.fi

.TP
.B Amend the commit message of the most recent pending changelist:
.nf
$ gfp commit --amend -m "feat(parser): add JSON and YAML configuration loader"
.fi

.TP
.B Amend a specific pending changelist:
.nf
$ gfp commit --amend -c 12345 -m "fix: resolve edge-case in path escaping"
.fi

